# {{ ansible_managed }}
# Included from the tail of abstractions/libvirt-qemu, the supported hook for
# site-local additions.
#
# Write access is required, not just read. virt-aa-helper builds each domain's
# profile from its XML and can only whitelist paths it can resolve — but this
# provider emits guest disks as <disk type='volume'> naming a pool and volume,
# not a path, and the helper does not resolve those. So no per-guest rule is
# generated for them at all, and the disk is denied on open-for-write.
#
# The trade-off is real: this grants every confined qemu process access to the
# whole pool, so AppArmor no longer isolates one guest's disk from another's.
# The alternative is worse — <disk type='file'> would resolve, but this
# provider hardcodes the driver to raw for any path it is given, and would
# hand qemu a qcow2 to interpret as a raw device (see disk_def.go:22 and
# domain.go:620 in v0.8.3). Silent corruption beats a clean permission error.
{{ libvirt_pool_path }}/** rwk,
